#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115045 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a227c7a8-977d-54b0-9409-d364da03656f" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Mean of a Data Set From the Sum"}] :question/id #uuid "22668678-c7e1-5a16-9dc0-17cf153ad4cc" :question/is-example true :question/math-academy-id "e-7580" :question/problem "Given a data set with $12$ data points and $\\displaystyle \\sum_{i=1}^{12} x_i = 96$, compute $\\overline{x}$." :question/worked-solution "If we have a data set that consists of the points $x_1, x_2, \\ldots, x_n$, then the mean is denoted by $\\overline{x}$ and is given by the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\overline{x} = \\dfrac{1}{n} \\sum_{i=1}^n x_i\n$$\n\nSubstituting $n=12$ and\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle \\sum_{i=1}^{12} x_i = 96\n$$\n\nwe get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx^(―) &= \\frac{1}{12} \\cdot 96 = 8\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115046 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "adfc527d-4347-5741-a81c-fa91c50d5d74" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Mean of a Data Set"}] :question/id #uuid "464f0fba-24f1-5c96-ab01-0f4633ef99d0" :question/is-example true :question/math-academy-id "e-7581" :question/problem "What is the mean of the following data set?\n$9, \\: 10, \\: 8, \\: 11, \\: 12$" :question/worked-solution "If we have a data set that consists of the points $x_1, x_2, \\ldots, x_n$, then the mean is denoted by $\\overline{x}$ and is given by the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\overline{x} = \\dfrac{1}{n} \\sum_{i=1}^n x_i\n$$\n\nHere, there are $n=5$ data points. Adding up all the points in the data set, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∑_(i = 1)^(5)x_{i} &= 9 + 10 + 8 + 11 + 12 \\\\\n&= 50\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the mean is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx^(―) &= \\frac{1}{n}∑_(i = 1)^(n)x_{i} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{5} \\cdot 50 \\\\\n&= 10\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115047 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b346e7e1-b641-5a97-9677-84a0ff6ab2dc" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Missing Values in a Data Set Given the Mean"}] :question/id #uuid "616a772d-6ab6-51e9-b5b6-9cd25224727b" :question/is-example true :question/math-academy-id "e-7582" :question/problem "Given that the mean of the following data set is $9$, find the value of $a$:\n$5, \\: 3, \\: a, \\: a, \\: a, \\: 7$" :question/worked-solution "If we have a data set that consists of the points $x_1, x_2, \\ldots, x_n$, then the mean is denoted by $\\overline{x}$ and is given by the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\overline{x} = \\dfrac{1}{n} \\sum_{i=1}^n x_i\n$$\n\nHere, there are $n=6$ data points. Adding up all the points in the data set, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∑_(i = 1)^(6)x_{i} &= 5 + 3 + a + a + a + 7 \\\\\n&= 15 + 3a\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the mean is given by the expression\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx^(―) &= \\frac{1}{n}∑_(i = 1)^(n)x_{i} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{6} \\cdot (15 + 3a) \\\\\n&= \\frac{15 + 3a}{6}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since we're told that\n\n$$\n\\overline{x} = 9\n$$\n\nwe have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n9 &= \\frac{15 + 3a}{6} \\\\\n54 &= 15 + 3a \\\\\n39 &= 3a \\\\\na &= 13\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115880 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "adfc527d-4347-5741-a81c-fa91c50d5d74" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Mean of a Data Set"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a9f809f5-c19e-56e5-8da0-bee361ecd6b5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186114652} {:answer/id #uuid "eb8ac752-2c21-5197-85f8-a3dcfda5a10a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186114653} {:answer/id #uuid "593cbf32-76d5-5eab-853c-3defb5a9d9d0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186114654} {:answer/id #uuid "5b308a58-affe-522b-ac05-11e47f43a0d1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6.3"